<title>INDIA: India approves Mobil's proposal to set up jetty.</title>
<headline>India approves Mobil's proposal to set up jetty.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>India on Thursday approved a proposal of U.S. Mobil International Petroleum Corporation to construct a jetty and port terminal for liquified petroleum gas (LPG) in the southern Kerala state, a government statement said.</p>
<p>Mobil will hold a foreign equity of 70 percent amounting to 117 million rupees, the statement said.</p>
<p>The government also approved a proposal of India's Tata Exports to make lubricants in Bombay, the statement said.</p>
<p>Tata exports will have an equity of 50 percent amounting to 65 million rupees, it said.</p>
</text>
